Modifications to Kraken API 5.5.1:

1. Compiled with javac --release 11 (class file version 55) instead of the
   upstream Java 17 toolchain.
2. The login package, the login hook class, and the break-handler package are
   not compiled into the sideload jar. That code reads the RuneLite credentials
   file or exists only to call it.
3. GameHooks and HooksLoader no longer map or return the login hook group, so
   loading hooks does not require the login hook class. hooks.json itself is
   the unmodified 5.5.1 resource, mapped for RuneLite 1.13.8 revision 243.
   No hook names were rewritten.
4. ClickScheduler still calls Client.getAccountHash(), through reflection, so
   the class file does not name the Jagex interface that declares that method.
   The method and its result are unchanged.

RuneLite client classes are not bundled. They are provided by the running client.
